+"""Verified [1,1]-Hamiltonicity generator for arXiv:2405.16270.
+
+The paper defines [a,b]-Hamiltonicity by a spanning closed walk whose visit
+count at every vertex is in [a,b].  The case a=b=1 is exactly Hamiltonicity.
+This module samples a spanning cycle first, adds one bounded-degree decoy edge
+at every vertex, and then randomly relabels the graph.  The planted cycle is
+therefore known without solving the generated instance.
