The audit found a material flaw in the existing evidence: its “standard” exact attack only enumerates perfect matchings and checks connectivity at leaves. Adding the standard forced-edge propagation and premature-subtour pruning solves the sampled `n=120` graphs in 40–19,012 branch nodes (roughly 0.01–6.6 s in an initial check). I’m incorporating that stronger attack and testing every rung; if it succeeds on any of the required eight seeds, Track A cannot ship at that rung.
