The post-cap probe found a viable correction: the prior module overcounted the compact graph route as `2n` arithmetic operations. A cycle witness requires one next-edge decision per vertex after the decomposition is recognized, so up to 256 vertices can still satisfy both the 256-atom and 300-operation caps. At `n=252`, the strengthened standard attack failed on 8/8 seeds. I’m testing nearby rungs with a larger node budget before deciding whether this supports a repaired Track A module.
