codex
The last cap-compliant rung (`n=256`) still failed the domain attack on 1/8 seeds, so size escalation is exhausted. I’m not hiding that result or declaring `cap_bound` yet: there is still a construction axis available—decoy distribution. I’m tuning page membership to retain the hard nested matching structure while eliminating the exact parity signature, and I’ll reject or park the family if no setting clears both the construction-specific spectral attack and the standard search.
