codex
A broad 20–25% page mix removed too much of the hard nested structure: the standard search still found witnesses at both `n=220` and `n=256`. I’m testing the remaining bounded axis—a constant four-vertex exchange per page—which breaks the exact eigenvector on every shipping seed but otherwise stays close to the original hard distribution. I’ll also test a repair-oriented spectral heuristic, since a small perturbation must not merely turn an exact leak into an approximate one.
exec
/bin/bash -lc "python3 -u - <<'PY'
