--- a/README.md
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1,141 +0,0 @@
-# arXiv:2405.16270 — bounded-degree multiple-Hamiltonicity generator
-
-Status: all local gates pass at the `easy` shipping preset. The required
-multi-vendor hardening and G9 diagnostics are **not scored**: the configured
-OpenRouter credential returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded” on every redraw.
-Those errors are preserved in the harness-owned transcripts and are not counted
-as model failures, so this result is locally verified but not yet shippable.
-
-| Profile field | Value |
-|---|---|
-| Track | A — structural hardness |
-| Native domain | combinatorics |
-| Object regime | finite discrete |
-| Computational core | graph |
-| Certificate form | integer tuple (normalized cyclic vertex order) |
-| Intended intuition | decomposition: in a cubic graph a Hamilton cycle is the complement of a perfect matching; the plant also has a hidden two-page noncrossing order |
-| Domain essentiality | native |
-| Reduction | none |
-
-## Problem and trust
-
-This module instantiates Definition 1 of Liu, Sheffield, and Westover,
-[“Complexity of Multiple-Hamiltonicity in Graphs of Bounded Degree”](https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.16270).
-The solver receives a simple undirected 3-regular graph and must exhibit a closed
-walk visiting every vertex exactly once—the paper's native `[1,1]-HAM` witness.
-The checker exactly tests normalization, permutation membership, every traversed
-edge, and the closing edge; it accepts any valid Hamilton cycle and never reads
-the planted answer.
-
-Generation is inverse and costs `O(n)`: sample the cycle first, add one decoy
-edge at every vertex using two independently sampled noncrossing page matchings,
-then apply a uniform vertex permutation and shuffle the edges. The certificate
-is the planted cyclic order carried through that relabelling; it is never found
-by solving the generated graph. A planted edge and decoy edge have the same
-one-edge marginal after relabelling, and every vertex has degree three.
-
-## Why Track A
-
-Section 2, Theorem 1 proves `[a,b]-HAM` NP-hard on odd `d`-regular graphs when
-`b<d`; this family uses `d=3` and `a=b=1`. It avoids the same section's easy
-Eulerian regime (`b>=d` for odd regular graphs), Section 3's linear tree
-algorithm, its polynomial high-ratio maximum-degree regimes, and Section 4's
-polynomial directed degree-three equality case.
-
-That theorem is worst-case, not an average-case theorem for this generator.
-Distributional evidence therefore comes from G5/G6. The standard exact attack
-branches on the perfect matching complementary to a cubic Hamilton cycle, adds
-forced-edge propagation and premature-subtour pruning, and repeats after random
-vertex relabellings. At `n=220` it exhausted 120,012 nodes on each of eight seeds
-(960,096 total; 194.403 seconds) without a witness. This stronger attack had
-solved 7/8 instances at the discarded `n=120` rung, which is why the ladder was
-moved upward rather than trusting the original weak brancher.
-
-## Worked demo
-
-`make_instance(n=8, seed=0)` produces the complete edge list:
-
-```text
-2-3 0-1 3-7 1-7 4-5 1-3 5-6 0-4 0-5 4-6 2-7 2-6
-```
-
-The answer `<answer>[0, 1, 7, 3, 2, 6, 5, 4]</answer>` gives every vertex once,
-starts at 0, fixes reversal by putting the smaller neighbour of 0 second, and
-uses a listed edge cyclically. `verify(inst, answer)` returns `(True, "ok")`;
-dropping the last vertex returns `(False, "wrong_length:7_expected_8")`. The demo
-has 4 valid normalized cycles among 2,520 normalized permutations and is
-hand-solvable.
-
-## Difficulty presets
-
-| Preset | `n` | Candidate-space bits (approx.) | Answer atoms | Intended decisions | Status |
-|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
-| demo | 8 | 12 | 8 | 8 | paper illustration |
-| easy | 220 | 1391 | 220 | 220 | shipping; local gates pass |
-| medium | 240 | 1548 | 240 | 240 | escalation |
-| hard | 256 | 1675 | 256 | 256 | last rung under the atom cap |
-
-`SHIPPING_DIFFICULTY = "easy"`. Beyond `n=256` the full spanning-cycle witness
-exceeds the 256-atom cap, so `escalate()` returns `"cap_bound"`.
-
-## Local gates
-
-| Gate | Result | Measurement |
-|---|---|---|
-| G1 | pass | 16/16 preset–seed plants verify; all answers JSON round-trip |
-| G2 | pass | 5/5 corruptions rejected with five distinct reason codes |
-| G3 | pass | prose/fence/tag response round-trips; garbage returns `None` |
-| G4 | pass | 0/200,000 normalized random permutations; 11.046 s |
-| G5 | pass | shipping density 0/200,000; demo exact 4/2,520; baseline 960,096 nodes / 194.403 s |
-| G6 | pass | six attacks, each 0/8 successes at shipping |
-| G7 | pass | doubled `n=440` instance builds and verifies |
-| G8 | pass | 60/60 invariance checks, 60/60 transported witnesses, 20/20 unrelated keys distinct |
-| G9(c) | pass | 771 chars, 193 estimated tokens, 220 atoms, 220 intended decisions |
-
-The G6 panel contains label-order guessing, local triangle/four-cycle scoring,
-constrained greedy walking, 64 randomized restarts, spectral circular seriation,
-and the propagated exact perfect-matching/complement search.
-
-## Oracle loop and G9 arms
-
-No row is a solve or a model failure. Each arm made four redraws and every call
-failed before inference with HTTP 403, so the harness issued no verdict.
-
-| Arm | Preset | Scored solved/attempts | Calls made | Outcome |
-|---|---|---:|---:|---|
-| bare | easy (`n=220`) | 0/0 | 4 | OpenRouter key-limit errors |
-| structural hint | easy (`n=220`) | 0/0 | 4 | OpenRouter key-limit errors |
-| placebo hint | easy (`n=220`) | 0/0 | 4 | OpenRouter key-limit errors |
-
-Hinted-minus-placebo is unavailable, not evidence of zero effect. Once the key
-is replenished, rerun all three arms and copy their scored counts into
-`G9_ORACLE_RESULTS`; answer size and the intended route already satisfy G9(c).
-
-## Use
-
-```python
-import json
-import gen_2405_16270 as g
-
-inst = g.make_instance(**g.DIFFICULTY[g.SHIPPING_DIFFICULTY], seed=42)
-text = "<answer>" + json.dumps(inst["answer"]) + "</answer>"
-answer = g.parse_answer(text)
-assert g.verify(inst, answer) == (True, "ok")
-```
-
-From the repository root, emit with `bash scripts/emit.sh 2405.16270 20`. After
-replenishing `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`, rerun the bare arm from this directory with
-`python3 ../../scripts/harden.py gen_2405_16270.py`; run structural and placebo
-modes only in their separate scratch directories because the harness overwrites
-its transcript.
-
-## Caveats
-
-The paper supplies worst-case hardness only. The 0/200,000 guess rate is under a
-uniform prior on normalized vertex permutations; it does not model a solver
-conditioning on graph edges. The exact attack is bounded, and no full planar
-embedding/dynamic-programming implementation, SAT/ILP encoding, or specialized
-planar Hamiltonicity solver was available. The canonical key is a strong
-distance-profile invariant, not a complete graph-isomorphism canonical form.
-Most importantly, there is no multi-vendor no-tool evidence until the credential
-limit is fixed; this directory must not be submitted as hardened before then.
