The module uses the paper’s native `[1,1]-HAM` problem on cubic graphs, inside Theorem 1’s NP-hard regime. Instances are inverse-generated around a known Hamilton cycle. [Paper full text](https://arxiv.org/html/2405.16270v1)

Local results:

- All G1–G9(c) gates pass.
- Random guesses: 0/200,000.
- Seven adversarial attacks: all 0/8.
- Strongest baseline: 960,096 nodes, 191.04 seconds, 0/8 solved.
- Answer: 899 characters, 252 atoms, approximately 225 tokens.
- An earlier spectral leakage was discovered, reproduced, and removed.

Blocker: all 12 harness calls returned OpenRouter HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded,” yielding 0 scored attempts. The transcripts correctly preserve those errors without treating them as model failures. Replenish `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` and rerun the bare, structural, and placebo harness arms to finish STEP 4.
